<title>USA: Mitchell Energy selling development for $543 million.</title>
<headline>Mitchell Energy selling development for $543 million.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitchell Energy &amp; Development Corp. said Thursday it agreed to sell its Woodlands Corp. property for $543 million to a real estate partnership that includes a Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co. affiliate.</p>
<p>Mitchell Energy, based in Texas, is selling the Woodlands development to Crescent Real Estate Equities Co., one of the country's largest real estate investment trusts, and Morgan Stanley Real Estate Fund II LP.</p>
<p>Mitchell, one of the country's largest independent natural gas producers, said it expects to report a loss of at least $55 million from the transaction in the second quarter.</p>
<p>The sale is subject to final reviews and approval by regulators, the company said. Closing is expected in 30 to 45 days, it added.</p>
